cess into a continuous score and gives more signal.\n3. **Task-specific quality metric** (tertiary) — wiping: mean force deviation from target. Bottle: smoothness of rotation. Only if it tells a story.\n\nThe partial success score is especially valuable because at 25% data, you'll likely see many partial failures. Binary success rate alone would just show \"0% success\" and you'd lose all signal. A continuous score lets you show *\"instrumentation pretrained reaches 70% task completion at 25% data vs. 30% for from-scratch\"* even if neither fully succeeds.\n\nCan you define a partial success score for each task?\n\n| Task | Partial success metric |\n|---|---|\n| Rubber plugs | Insertion depth (normalized 0-1) from circuit resistance or depth sensor |\n| Bottle opening | Cap rotation angle / total required angle (from LDR or joint angles) |\n| Disk wiping | Area covered / total area (from load cell contact duration) |\n\nDo these work, or do you have better proposals?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8","usage":{"input":29215,"output":1092,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30307,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782821491742,"responseId":"chatcmpl-87b1f5193145134e"}}
