s) | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 20 | ✓ | ✓ | If 90%+ → N=20. If <60% → continue |\n| 2 | 40 | ✓ | ✓ | Same check |\n| 3 | 60 | ✓ | ✓ | Same check |\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | Until 90% or plateau |\n\n**Plateau detection:** Success rate doesn't improve by more than 5% over two consecutive iterations.\n\n**Risk:** N could end up very different across tasks. Plugs might need 30 episodes, wiping might need 100. That's fine — it's task-dependent, which is honest. But it means the 25% condition represents very different absolute amounts of data across tasks.\n\n**My recommendation: Cap N at a reasonable max (e.g., 100 episodes).** If from-scratch doesn't reach 90% at 100 episodes, accept the plateau value as the task ceiling. This bounds the worst-case data collection effort.\n\nDoes this iterative protocol work for you, or did you envision a different approach to finding N?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8","usage":{"input":31371,"output":695,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32066,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782822309480,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8a3460cfbb1afc12"}}
