Random |\n| **Instrumentation pretrained** | Pretrained on LDR prediction | Random |\n| **Generic pretrained** | **???** | Random |\n\nThe generic pretrained variant should match the instrumentation variant in **which encoder is pretrained**, differing only in **what it's pretrained on**:\n\n- **Instrumentation pretrained**: image encoder pretrained on LDR labels (task-specific)\n- **Generic pretrained**: image encoder pretrained on ImageNet (task-agnostic)\n\nBoth audio encoders are random. Both get fine-tuned during policy training.\n\n**This is the correct setup** — it isolates the question: *\"Does pretraining on instrumentation labels help more than pretraining on generic data?\"*\n\n**But what if the suitability metric picks audio for a task?** Then:\n- Instrumentation pretrained: **audio** encoder pretrained on instrument labels\n- Generic pretrained: **audio** encoder pretrained on AudioSet\n\nThe generic-pretrained variant always mirrors the instrumentation variant's encoder choice. The only difference is the pretraining data source.\n\nIs this how you envisioned it? Or did you have something else in mind for the generic baseline?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8","usage":{"input":32857,"output":597,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33454,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782823615137,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8af8406d7eab20ec"}}
