{"type":"message","id":"6bce9a64","parentId":"37f0020c","timestamp":"2026-06-30T12:48:37.433Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user confirmed the setup. Let me lock this in and think about what's left.\n\nWe've covered a LOT. Let me review what's remaining:\n\n1. Statistical analysis - how to report significance\n2. What if both modalities have similar suitability scores?\n3. The full experimental pipeline summary\n4. Any other overlooked aspects\n\nLet me ask about statistical analysis and tie-off remaining loose ends. Actually, let me think about whether there are more substantive design questions or if we're close to wrapping up.\n\nRemaining open items:\n- Statistical significance testing (t-tests? bootstrap?)\n- What to do if suitability scores are tied between audio and image\n- Demo filtering (only successful episodes for training?)\n- The \"from scratch\" variant's audio encoder - is it always random, or could it also benefit from some pretraining?\n\nActually, the user said \"ask questions one at a time\" so let me pick the most impactful remaining question. I think demo filtering is important - do you train only on successful demonstrations, or include failures too?\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nLocked in: **Generic pretrained mirrors instrumentation variant's encoder choice, differs only in pretraining source (ImageNet/AudioSet vs. instrumentation labels).**\n\n---\n\n## Question 18: Demo filtering — do you train only on successful demonstrations, or include failed ones too?\n\nDuring teleop data collection, not all episodes will be successful. Some buttons won't get pressed, some bottles won't fully open, etc.\n\n**Option A — Successful demos only.** Filter out failed episodes. Train only on trajectories that achieved the goal. This is the standard in imitation learning (BC/DP learn from expert behavior).\n\n**Option B — All demos (success + failure).** Include everything. The policy learns from both good and bad behavior. Usually performs worse but is more robust to distribution shift.\n\n**My recommendation: Option A — successful demos only.** Here's why:\n- Your success criterion is well-defined (instrumentation signal)\n- Filtering is automatic (check instrumentation at end of episode)\n- Standard practice in the field (reviewers expect it)\n- Cleaner signal for the \"data efficiency\" claim: \"with 25% of *successful* demos, pretrained reaches X% success\"\n\n**Important consequence:** The iterative N-finding protocol produces N *successful* episodes. Failed episodes during collection are discarded and don't count toward N. This means you might collect 120 episodes to get N=100 successful ones. Factor that into your time estimates.\n\nDoes this work for you?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8","usage":{"input":33466,"output":533,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33999,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782823707978,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9b1137de22babd93"}}
